**Algorithm (pseudocode)**

```text
Initialise(MaxNoOfStars, NoOfSpaces, NoOfStars)
REPEAT
    OutputLeadingSpaces(NoOfSpaces)
    OutputLineOfStars(NoOfStars)
    Adjust(NoOfSpaces, NoOfStars)
UNTIL NoOfStars > MaxNoOfStars
```

The loop body runs once per line. The test is made after the body (REPEAT ... UNTIL), so the base line, where `NoOfStars = MaxNoOfStars`, is printed; the loop stops only when `Adjust` has produced `NoOfStars = MaxNoOfStars + 2`.

**Complete program (ANSI C)** - the three variables are global, the procedures of Task 2 are called with their addresses:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

/* global variables (Task 3) */
int MaxNoOfStars;
int NoOfSpaces;
int NoOfStars;

/* the parameters of the procedures below carry the names of the question; they are pointers so that
   the procedures can change the global variables (call by reference, like var in Pascal) */

void Initialise(int *MaxNoOfStars, int *NoOfSpaces, int *NoOfStars)
{
    int base = 0;

    printf("Enter the size of the base (an odd positive integer): ");
    scanf("%d", &base);
    while (base < 1 || base % 2 == 0)       /* reject even or non-positive values */
    {
        printf("The base must be an odd positive integer. Try again: ");
        scanf("%d", &base);
    }
    *MaxNoOfStars = base;                   /* stars on the last line (the base) */
    *NoOfSpaces = (base - 1) / 2;           /* the first line is centred over the base */
    *NoOfStars = 1;                         /* the first line has a single star */
}

void OutputLeadingSpaces(int nSpaces)
{
    int i;

    for (i = 1; i <= nSpaces; i++)
        putchar(' ');
}

void OutputLineOfStars(int nStars)
{
    int i;

    for (i = 1; i <= nStars; i++)
        putchar('*');
    putchar('\n');                          /* end of the line */
}

void Adjust(int *NoOfSpaces, int *NoOfStars)
{
    *NoOfSpaces = *NoOfSpaces - 1;          /* one blank less ... */
    *NoOfStars = *NoOfStars + 2;            /* ... and two more stars */
}

int main(void)
{
    Initialise(&MaxNoOfStars, &NoOfSpaces, &NoOfStars);
    do
    {
        OutputLeadingSpaces(NoOfSpaces);
        OutputLineOfStars(NoOfStars);
        Adjust(&NoOfSpaces, &NoOfStars);
    } while (NoOfStars <= MaxNoOfStars);    /* "until NoOfStars > MaxNoOfStars" */
    return 0;
}
```

In C the condition "until `NoOfStars > MaxNoOfStars`" becomes `while (NoOfStars <= MaxNoOfStars)` at the bottom of a `do ... while` loop (a `do ... while` repeats WHILE its condition is true, whereas REPEAT ... UNTIL stops WHEN it becomes true).

**Trace for a base of 5**

| Line printed | NoOfSpaces | NoOfStars | After Adjust | Test `NoOfStars <= 5` |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `  *` | 2 | 1 | (1, 3) | true |
| ` ***` | 1 | 3 | (0, 5) | true |
| `*****` | 0 | 5 | (-1, 7) | false: stop |

